E('space race', 'The Space Race was a Cold War competition between the US and the Soviet Union in spaceflight.', 'It ran from 1957 to about 1975.',
  'The USSR launched Sputnik 1, the first artificial satellite, on 4 October 1957.', 'Yuri Gagarin became the first person in space in 1961.', 'The US landed Apollo 11 on the Moon in 1969.', 'The joint Apollo–Soyuz mission in 1975 marked a thaw.',
  'It drove huge advances in technology and science.')
E('sputnik|sputnik 1', 'Sputnik 1 was the first artificial satellite.', 'The Soviet Union launched it on 4 October 1957.',
  'It was a metal sphere 58 centimetres across with four antennae.', 'It sent out radio beeps that people around the world could hear.', 'It burned up in the atmosphere in January 1958.',
  'It shocked the US and started the Space Race.')
E('yuri gagarin|gagarin|first man in space|first person in space', 'Yuri Gagarin was a Soviet pilot and the first human in space.', 'He flew on 12 April 1961.',
  'His spacecraft, Vostok 1, orbited Earth once in about 108 minutes.', 'He became a worldwide celebrity.', 'He died in a jet crash in 1968.',
  '12 April is celebrated as Cosmonautics Day in Russia.')
E('valentina tereshkova|first woman in space', 'Valentina Tereshkova was a Soviet cosmonaut and the first woman in space.', 'She flew in June 1963.',
  'She orbited Earth 48 times in Vostok 6.', 'She had been a textile worker and amateur parachutist.', 'She later became a politician.',
  'She remains the only woman to have flown a solo space mission.')
E('apollo 11|moon landing|neil armstrong|buzz aldrin|first man on the moon|apollo program|apollo', 'Apollo 11 was the first mission to land humans on the Moon.', 'Neil Armstrong stepped onto the Moon on 20 July 1969.',
  'The crew were Neil Armstrong, Buzz Aldrin and Michael Collins, who stayed in orbit.', 'Armstrong said, “That’s one small step for man, one giant leap for mankind.”', 'Their lunar module was called Eagle.', 'About 600 million people watched on TV.', 'Twelve people walked on the Moon in six Apollo landings, the last in 1972.', 'Apollo 13 famously suffered an explosion in 1970 but returned safely.',
  'It is one of humanity’s greatest achievements.')
E('international space station|iss|space station', 'The International Space Station is a large orbiting laboratory.', 'Construction began in 1998, and people have lived aboard continuously since November 2000.',
  'It was built by the US, Russia, Europe, Japan and Canada.', 'It orbits Earth about every 90 minutes.', 'It is about the size of a football pitch.', 'Astronauts study how space affects the body.',
  'It is one of the largest international scientific projects ever.')
E('space shuttle|challenger|columbia disaster', 'The Space Shuttle was NASA’s reusable spacecraft.', 'It flew from 1981 to 2011.',
  'It launched satellites and helped build the ISS.', 'Challenger broke apart after launch in 1986, killing seven astronauts.', 'Columbia broke apart on re-entry in 2003, killing seven more.', 'It flew 135 missions.',
  'It showed both the promise and the risks of spaceflight.')
E('voyager|voyager 1|voyager 2|golden record', 'The Voyager probes are two NASA spacecraft exploring the outer solar system and beyond.', 'Both launched in 1977.',
  'They flew past Jupiter and Saturn; Voyager 2 also visited Uranus and Neptune.', 'Voyager 1 entered interstellar space in 2012.', 'Each carries a Golden Record with sounds and images of Earth.', 'Voyager 1 took the “Pale Blue Dot” photo of Earth in 1990.',
  'They are the farthest human-made objects from Earth.')
E('vincent van gogh|van gogh|starry night', 'Vincent van Gogh was a Dutch Post-Impressionist painter.', 'He lived from 1853 to 1890.',
  'He painted The Starry Night in 1889.', 'He made about 2,100 artworks in about a decade.', 'He sold very few paintings in his lifetime.', 'He struggled with mental illness and famously cut off part of his ear.', 'He died at 37.',
  'He is now one of the most famous and influential artists ever.')
E('picasso|pablo picasso|cubism|guernica', 'Pablo Picasso was a Spanish artist, one of the most influential of the 20th century.', 'He lived from 1881 to 1973.',
  'He co-founded Cubism with Georges Braque.', 'His painting Guernica (1937) shows the horror of a bombing in the Spanish Civil War.', 'He went through a “Blue Period” and a “Rose Period”.', 'He made tens of thousands of works.',
  'He changed what art could look like.')
E('impressionism|claude monet|monet', 'Impressionism was an art movement that captured light and everyday moments.', 'It began in France in the 1860s and 1870s.',
  'Claude Monet’s painting Impression, Sunrise gave it its name.', 'Artists painted outdoors with quick, visible brushstrokes.', 'Other Impressionists include Renoir, Degas and Morisot.', 'Monet painted his water lilies at Giverny.',
  'It opened the way to modern art.')
E('frida kahlo|kahlo', 'Frida Kahlo was a Mexican painter famous for her self-portraits.', 'She lived from 1907 to 1954.',
  'A bus accident at 18 left her in pain for life.', 'She painted 55 self-portraits.', 'Her work draws on Mexican culture.', 'She married the muralist Diego Rivera.',
  'She is an icon of art, identity and resilience.')
E('rembrandt|the night watch', 'Rembrandt was a Dutch painter of the 17th century.', 'He lived from 1606 to 1669.',
  'He was a master of light and shadow.', 'His most famous painting is The Night Watch (1642).', 'He painted many self-portraits throughout his life.', 'He went bankrupt despite his fame.',
  'He is one of the greatest painters in history.')
E('beethoven|ludwig van beethoven', 'Ludwig van Beethoven was a German composer, one of the greatest in Western music.', 'He lived from 1770 to 1827.',
  'He bridged the Classical and Romantic eras.', 'He began losing his hearing in his late twenties.', 'He composed his Ninth Symphony while almost completely deaf.', 'Its “Ode to Joy” is now the anthem of the European Union.', 'His Fifth Symphony opens with four famous notes.',
  'His music is still among the most performed in the world.')
E('mozart|wolfgang amadeus mozart', 'Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was an Austrian composer of the Classical era.', 'He lived from 1756 to 1791.',
  'He was a child prodigy who composed from age five.', 'He wrote over 600 works.', 'His operas include The Magic Flute and The Marriage of Figaro.', 'He died at 35, leaving his Requiem unfinished.',
  'He is one of the most celebrated composers ever.')
E('bach|johann sebastian bach', 'Johann Sebastian Bach was a German composer of the Baroque era.', 'He lived from 1685 to 1750.',
  'He wrote the Brandenburg Concertos and the Mass in B minor.', 'He was a brilliant organist.', 'He had twenty children.', 'He was more famous as an organist than a composer in his lifetime.',
  'Many musicians consider him the greatest composer of all.')
E('the beatles|beatles', 'The Beatles were an English rock band, the best-selling music act in history.', 'They formed in Liverpool in 1960 and split in 1970.',
  'The members were John Lennon, Paul McCartney, George Harrison and Ringo Starr.', '“Beatlemania” swept Britain and the US.', 'Their albums include Sgt. Pepper’s Lonely Hearts Club Band and Abbey Road.', 'Lennon and McCartney wrote most of their songs.',
  'They transformed popular music and youth culture.')
E('elvis presley|elvis', 'Elvis Presley was an American singer known as the “King of Rock and Roll”.', 'He lived from 1935 to 1977.',
  'His hits include Heartbreak Hotel and Hound Dog.', 'He starred in 31 films.', 'He served in the US Army in Germany.', 'He lived at Graceland in Memphis.',
  'He is one of the best-selling solo artists ever.')
E('michael jackson', 'Michael Jackson was an American singer and dancer called the “King of Pop”.', 'He lived from 1958 to 2009.',
  'He began in the Jackson 5 as a child.', 'His album Thriller (1982) is often cited as the best-selling album of all time.', 'He made the moonwalk famous.',
  'His music videos changed pop culture.')
E('jane austen|pride and prejudice', 'Jane Austen was an English novelist.', 'She lived from 1775 to 1817.',
  'Her novels include Pride and Prejudice, Sense and Sensibility and Emma.', 'She wrote with wit about marriage, money and class.', 'Her books were published anonymously.',
  'She is one of the most loved writers in English.')
E('charles dickens|dickens|a christmas carol|oliver twist', 'Charles Dickens was an English novelist of the Victorian era.', 'He lived from 1812 to 1870.',
  'His novels include Oliver Twist, A Christmas Carol, Great Expectations and David Copperfield.', 'As a boy he worked in a factory while his father was in debtors’ prison.', 'His books exposed poverty and injustice.', 'Many were published in instalments.',
  'He created characters like Scrooge who are still famous.')
E('tolstoy|leo tolstoy|war and peace', 'Leo Tolstoy was a Russian writer, one of the greatest novelists.', 'He lived from 1828 to 1910.',
  'He wrote War and Peace and Anna Karenina.', 'War and Peace is set during Napoleon’s invasion of Russia.', 'He later championed non-violence, influencing Gandhi.',
  'He is often ranked among the greatest authors ever.')
E('george orwell|orwell|1984|animal farm', 'George Orwell was an English writer known for warning against totalitarianism.', 'He lived from 1903 to 1950; his real name was Eric Blair.',
  'He wrote Animal Farm (1945) and Nineteen Eighty-Four (1949).', 'Nineteen Eighty-Four gave us “Big Brother” and “thought police”.', 'He fought in the Spanish Civil War.',
  '“Orwellian” describes oppressive, controlling governments.')
E('tolkien|j r r tolkien|lord of the rings|the hobbit', 'J. R. R. Tolkien was an English writer and scholar, author of The Hobbit and The Lord of the Rings.', 'He lived from 1892 to 1973.',
  'He was a professor of Old English at Oxford.', 'The Hobbit came out in 1937.', 'The Lord of the Rings was published in 1954 and 1955.', 'He invented whole languages for his Elves.',
  'He is called the father of modern fantasy.')
E('homer simpson|the simpsons', 'The Simpsons is an American animated sitcom created by Matt Groening.', 'It first aired as a series in December 1989.',
  'It follows Homer, Marge, Bart, Lisa and Maggie in Springfield.', 'It is the longest-running American scripted primetime series.',
  'It is famous for satire and for seeming to predict future events.')
E('dante|divine comedy|dante alighieri', 'Dante Alighieri was an Italian poet, author of the Divine Comedy.', 'He lived from about 1265 to 1321.',
  'The Divine Comedy follows Dante through Hell, Purgatory and Paradise.', 'He wrote in Italian rather than Latin.', 'He was exiled from Florence.',
  'He is called the father of the Italian language.')
E('cervantes|don quixote', 'Miguel de Cervantes was a Spanish writer, author of Don Quixote.', 'He lived from 1547 to 1616.',
  'Don Quixote was published in two parts, in 1605 and 1615.', 'It follows a man who reads so many romances he decides to become a knight.', 'He tilts at windmills thinking they are giants.',
  'It is often called the first modern novel.')
